                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "a37e69c7-375f-4879-9715-4bc5b328ac67",
                        "entry_id": "ff745dae-63e7-3454-aff4-4857b4965fdf",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more censorious"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "81da93a0-6dc2-4861-b9de-31a0318e1be6",
                        "entry_id": "ff745dae-63e7-3454-aff4-4857b4965fdf",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most censorious"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c91c86eb-4157-3cf2-98c0-8e1622bed3f1",
                        "entry_id": "ff745dae-63e7-3454-aff4-4857b4965fdf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Addicted to censure and scolding; apt to blame or condemn; severe in making remarks on others, or on their writings or manners."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "522af7a1-368b-4a68-b9fe-6e1111b34717",
                                "sense_id": "c91c86eb-4157-3cf2-98c0-8e1622bed3f1",
                                "text": "Be not too rigidly Cenſorious, / A ſtring may jarr in the beſt Maſters hand, / And the moſt skilfull Archer miſs his aim; / But in a Poem elegantly writ, / I will not quarrel with a ſlight miſtake, / Such as our Natures frailty may excuſe; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bfde6532-206e-4934-b7f5-e66cef9fc42e",
                                "sense_id": "c91c86eb-4157-3cf2-98c0-8e1622bed3f1",
                                "text": "[S]he remembered the Countess of Rotheles's advice, and she well knew the very pointed words and looks Lady Allerton could assume when it suited her humour to be censorious, and was well aware that every particular of the evening's entertainment would be transmitted with a jaundiced tint to Rotheles Castle for the amusement and animadversion of her invalid brother."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "81450eb4-ee76-4a26-a561-a0920b77c9d0",
                                "sense_id": "c91c86eb-4157-3cf2-98c0-8e1622bed3f1",
                                "text": "But, my dear David, this world is a censorious place—as who should know it better than myself, who have lived ever since the days of my late departed father, God sain him! in a perfect spate of calumnies?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "98dc4464-3579-4778-b8e4-a8f2598bdd4e",
                                "sense_id": "c91c86eb-4157-3cf2-98c0-8e1622bed3f1",
                                "text": "But I'm guessing the girls didn't push for molestation charges because they were censorious prudes who would grow into knowing how to take such behaviour on the chin – they felt genuinely threatened, they took their concerns to court, and they deserved more than being told that they'd misread the situation all along."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cb5b9378-22ac-49c5-975e-fe07932876d4",
                                "sense_id": "c91c86eb-4157-3cf2-98c0-8e1622bed3f1",
                                "text": "Thanks to a censorious judge, the vile behaviour of the duke, a series of photographs showing the duchess performing fellatio on an unidentified man and her own altruistic, if high-handed, refusal to defend herself, the sexual ins and outs of this separation are a matter of incredibly detailed historical record."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2fcb73dc-febe-3079-a211-576c6ba3babe",
                        "entry_id": "ff745dae-63e7-3454-aff4-4857b4965fdf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Implying or expressing censure."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cb2cdc00-404c-4b69-8977-3690faf85116",
                                "sense_id": "2fcb73dc-febe-3079-a211-576c6ba3babe",
                                "text": "censorious remarks"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ba32d733-dd52-3c3e-b67b-8e51c3c419f5",
                        "entry_id": "ff745dae-63e7-3454-aff4-4857b4965fdf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Tending to engage in or support censorship."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "proscribed"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "349b4266-61db-4b97-a2b1-c7ee26f98f7f",
                                "sense_id": "ba32d733-dd52-3c3e-b67b-8e51c3c419f5",
                                "text": "Chick-Fil-A^([sic]) has survived and thrived because they served everyone AND refused to cater to the cancel culture. Now they’ve caved at the behest of the censorious Left. This is a terrible move and just the latest indicator that the center cannot hold."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a3078f33-e3d0-4122-9751-9df5cec28e89",
                                "sense_id": "ba32d733-dd52-3c3e-b67b-8e51c3c419f5",
                                "text": "Is there something in the California water that makes Silicon Valley's censorious dweebs so damned shameless?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5c9b78da-a7d1-40ec-a74d-a1eeb167b4ec",
                                "sense_id": "ba32d733-dd52-3c3e-b67b-8e51c3c419f5",
                                "text": "Pushed by militantly conservative activists — and heeding the demands of an increasingly censorious group of conservative voters — Republican lawmakers are, in states across the country, introducing bills that suppress debate and stifle discussion in favor of the rote memorization of approved facts."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "18ff2f89-baaf-43b2-8e94-122dc3fdcf05",
                                "sense_id": "ba32d733-dd52-3c3e-b67b-8e51c3c419f5",
                                "text": "Only seven new gag order bills have become law so far this year, but these include some of the most censorious laws to date. Nineteen states, home to 122 million Americans, now have some sort of educational gag order on the books. The entire year can be summarized in a single word: escalation."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
